// LB+falsedep+data -- load buffering where the first thread's write mentions
// its read but does not depend on it: r0 + 1 - r0 is 1 whatever r0 is. sMRD
// computes dependencies semantically, finds none, and allows it as it allows
// LB+data.lit. OCaml forbids it, as it forbids every load-buffering shape.
//
// The OCaml memory model (Dolan, Sivaramakrishnan & Madhavapeddy, PLDI 2018,
// section 6). An access in mode sc is to an atomic location, any other access
// non-atomic.
a := 0;
b := 0;
{
  r0 := a;
  b := r0 + 1 - r0
} ||| {
  r1 := b;
  a := r1
}
%%
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 1) [OCaml]
allow (r0 = 1 && r1 = 1) [smrd]
